description.narrative:
Major Programme IV - Culture
Supporting implementation of Strategic Objective 3, Outcome 4: "A world where culture in all its forms is protected and promoted", and in particular;
Output 4.4: Capacities of Member States and civil society strengthened to protect and promote the diversity of cultural expressions through dynamic, inclusive cultural industries, Creative Cities, and museums, and specifically;
4.4.CLT. 1 Number of Member States supported to develop new or revised policies, regulatory frameworks, measures and/or initiatives strengthening cultural and creative industries globally, including in the digital environment, in line with the 2005 Convention on the Protection and Promotion of the Diversity of Cultural Expression
4.4.CLT.2 Number of Member States supported to develop new or revised policies, regulatory frameworks, measures and/or initiatives improving the working conditions and the social and economic rights of artists and culture professionals, in line with the implementation of the 1980 Recommendation concerning the Status of the Artist with particular attention to gender equality and social inclusion
4.4.CLT.3 Number of Member States supported to implement policies, measures and programmes supporting inclusion and gender equality in the culture and creative sectors.
Major Programme V - Communication and Information
Supporting the implementation of Strategic Objective 3, Outcome 5: "A world where freedom of expression and the right and access to information are guaranteed to allow societies to manage today's transitions in a just and inclusive way".
Strategic Objective 3, Outcome 6: "A world of peace and inclusion, free from discrimination, disinformation and hate speech", and in particular;
Intersectoral Output 6.3.CI: Member States, education institutions, youth organizations, and media supported in adopting inclusive Media and Information Literacy policies and digital initiatives to build resilience to disinformation, misinformation, and hate speech.
Strategic Objective 4, Outcome 7: "A world where new technologies are developed and applied ethically for sustainable development and in respect of human rights and dignity", and in particular;
Intersectoral Output 7.1.CI: Member States and other stakeholders supported in developing and implementing ethical Al governance frameworks, policies and institutions incorporating human rights, gender equality and sustainability, building on the Recommendation on the Ethics of Al.
